{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 1, "compounds_kept": 1, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 14, "cost_per_unit": "Lexing costs one or more compiled-regex calls per position, plus generator and consume overhead. Each grouping pass costs 2 to 4 Python calls per node (a closure or lambda, then imt, match or tokens.__contains__), even when the pass's trigger token appears nowhere in the statement.", "deal_round": 2, "doubling": "Linear. Statements are independent and of fixed size, so doubling the script roughly doubles lexing and grouping time. Per-statement cost does not change.", "gap": "Each statement text is lexed twice (format, then parse of the same string). Many grouping passes do a full recursive walk that cannot change anything because no leaf could ever match. In this workload, typecasts, tzcasts, typed_literal (two passes), assignment, comments, align_comments and over are ", "least_work": "Lex each distinct text once. Walk the tree only for passes whose trigger token (::, :=, TZCast, a typed-literal opener, a comment, OVER, Keyword.Order) actually occurs in the statement, and visit each remaining node once per useful pass.", "library": "sqlparse", "run": 3, "unit_count": "get_tokens yields 66k tokens over 3 lexings: the whole-script split, then format and parse of each of 160 statements. That is about 22k tokens per lexing, roughly 138 per statement. Grouping runs on 320 statement trees (format plus parse), and each tree is walked by about 12 _group passes, 6 _group_", "unit_of_work": "One token visited by one stage: a lexer regex scan per character position, plus a grouping-pass visit per tree node. About 25 grouping passes run per statement."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 3, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "3abcfdec"}, {"lane": "name_the_problem", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "3abcfdec"}, {"lane": "leap", "served_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "view_sha": "3abcfdec"}, {"lane": "resolve_trade