{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 5, "cost_per_unit": "About 26 us cumulative per statement under the profiler (1.33 s / 51,200). That is roughly 20+ Python calls per statement: about 10 skip_chars calls, parse_key, parse_key_part, parse_key_value_pair, parse_value, Flags.is_ and get_or_create_nest root walks, plus tuple concatenation and slicing.", "deal_round": 1, "doubling": "Linear: twice the tables gives twice the statements and about twice the time. Per-statement cost depends on key and header depth, not document size.", "gap": "Most time is interpreter call overhead, not character work. Several tiny helper calls are made where one regex or one character test would do. The current table's nest and frozen state are recomputed from the root for every key, although they cannot change within a section.", "least_work": "Any correct parser must look at each source character once, do one dict insert per value, convert each scalar once and check redefinition per key. Locating the target table for keys in the same section needs no repeated work.", "library": "tomli", "run": 3, "unit_count": "51,200 key/value statements, 108,800 values, 67,200 parse_key, 70,400 parse_key_part, 502,400 skip_chars and 115,200 skip_comments_and_array_ws calls across 8 parses.", "unit_of_work": "One TOML statement, mostly a key/value line: key_value_rule runs 51,200 times (6,400 per parse x 8). Under it are 108,800 parse_value calls, counting array items and inline-table values."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 4, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "c7601090"}, {"lane": "leap", "served_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "view_sha": "c7601090"}, {"lane": "far", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "c7601090"}, {"lane": "assume_less", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "c7601090"}, {"lane": "recombine", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "c7601090"}, {"lane": "